{"title": "Stool of Hill Giant Strength", "pageid": 11599, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Stool_of_Hill_Giant_Strength", "categories": ["Transcripts", "Environmental objects"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Stool of Hill Giant Strength</b> is an interactable item on the top floor of the <a href=\"/wiki/Arcane_Tower\" title=\"Arcane Tower\">Arcane Tower</a>, in the far corner under the thatched roof. \n</p>\n<blockquote style=\"font-size:130%; font-family:Georgia;\"><i> You feel a surge of strength as you approach the chair - a curious effect. </i></blockquote>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Involvement\">Involvement</span></h2>\n<p>Characters who sit on the Stool of Hill Giant Strength gain <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Hill_Giant%27s_Might_(Condition)\" title=\"Hill Giant's Might (Condition)\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c9/Muscular_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Muscular_Condition_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/c/c9/Muscular_Condition_Icon.webp/38px-Muscular_Condition_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/c/c9/Muscular_Condition_Icon.webp/50px-Muscular_Condition_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Hill Giant's Might\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c9/Muscular_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Muscular_Condition_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/c/c9/Muscular_Condition_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Hill_Giant%27s_Might_(Condition)\" title=\"Hill Giant's Might (Condition)\">Hill Giant's Might</a>, a condition that sets their strength to 21. The character who sits on the stool will comment about feeling powerful while sitting on it, then note that the power is gone when they stand up.\n</p><p>Destroying the stool yields the <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-uncommon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Club_of_Hill_Giant_Strength\" title=\"Club of Hill Giant Strength\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/e/ea/Club_Unfaded_Icon.png/25px-Club_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/e/ea/Club_Unfaded_Icon.png/38px-Club_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/e/ea/Club_Unfaded_Icon.png/50px-Club_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/e/ea/Club_Unfaded_Icon.png/25px-Club_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/e/ea/Club_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Club_of_Hill_Giant_Strength\" title=\"Club of Hill Giant Strength\">Club of Hill Giant Strength</a>, a club that raises strength of the user to 19 as long they wield it.\n</p><p>A second stool of hill giant strength can be found in a smuggler's cave on the <a href=\"/wiki/Western_Beach\" title=\"Western Beach\">Western Beach</a> beneath <a href=\"/wiki/Rivington\" title=\"Rivington\">Rivington</a>, near to the chest where the <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-very-rare\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Bonespike_Boots\" title=\"Bonespike Boots\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/0/0b/Bonespike_Boots_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Bonespike_Boots_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/0/0b/Bonespike_Boots_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Bonespike_Boots_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/0/0b/Bonespike_Boots_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Bonespike_Boots_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/0/0b/Bonespike_Boots_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Bonespike_Boots_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/0/0b/Bonespike_Boots_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Bonespike_Boots\" title=\"Bonespike Boots\">Bonespike Boots</a> are found. This second stool is however non-functional: no dialogue or buff is received when sitting on it and destroying it does not provide a second club. It is unknown if its placement here is a mistake or intended to imply the smuggling of fake goods.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Dialogue\">Dialogue</span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-transcript\">\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Player character</dt><dd>\"What's this... feeling of <i>power?</i>\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Player character</dt><dd>\"It's gone. I felt so strong - where did that come from?\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Player character</dt><dd>\"That chair leg could make for a fine weapon...\"&nbsp;<span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-condition\"><i>(If destroyed)</i></span></dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-transcript\">\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Lae'zel</dt><dd>\"What is this <i>power</i>?\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Lae'zel</dt><dd>\"The power's gone. A most vexing chair...\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Lae'zel</dt><dd>\"It is no silver sword, but that chair leg may be a useful weapon.\"&nbsp;<span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-condition\"><i>(If destroyed)</i></span></dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-transcript\">\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Astarion</dt><dd>\"Well now, what's this? I feel <i>powerful</i>.\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Astarion</dt><dd>\"Damn it, it's gone...\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Astarion</dt><dd>\"This could do some damage. Waste not...\"&nbsp;<span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-condition\"><i>(If destroyed)</i></span></dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-transcript\">\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Gale</dt><dd>\"My, not only is this chair comfortable, it imbues its sitter with power!\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Gale</dt><dd>\"Hmmm. So if I stand, the power's gone. Sedentary magic I suppose that's called.\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Gale</dt><dd>\"Look at that. An unconventional weapon, but it might just be an effective one.\"&nbsp;<span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-condition\"><i>(If destroyed)</i></span></dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-transcript\">\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Karlach</dt><dd>\"Ohoho, I like this. I feel strong as hell.\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Karlach</dt><dd>\"Aw! Power's gone as soon as I stand up.\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Karlach</dt><dd>\"I could do some real damage with that chair leg.\"&nbsp;<span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-condition\"><i>(If destroyed)</i></span></dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-transcript\">\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Wyll</dt><dd>\"Holy... I feel <i>powerful.</i> Nice chair indeed.\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Wyll</dt><dd>\"And <i>poof</i> - the power's gone.\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Wyll</dt><dd>\"Hm - that chair leg might be good for smacking monsters around.\"&nbsp;<span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-condition\"><i>(If destroyed)</i></span></dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-transcript\">\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Shadowheart</dt><dd>\"This chair... I feel stronger just from sitting in it.\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Shadowheart</dt><dd>\"The strength vanishes as soon as I stand. Curious.\"</dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li><dl class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-line\"><dt>Shadowheart</dt><dd>\"Hmm. As much as I enjoy a sit-down, a strengthening bludgeon is more useful...\"&nbsp;<span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-condition\"><i>(If destroyed)</i></span></dd></dl></li></ul></li></ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h2>\n<ul><li>Patch 6 adjusted the location of the stool in Act 1, making it upright instead of laying on its side and moving it further into the corner. A non-magical stool was placed on its side in the Hill Giant Stool's old location.</li>\n<li>Since patch 6 (and through patch 8) sometimes destroying the stool does not drop the Club of Hill Giant Strength. A workaround that may help is to (1) sit on the Stool of Hill Giant Strength (2) get up and destroy the separate nearby stool lying on its side in front of a table (3) destroy the Stool of Hill Giant Strength. The Club of Hill Giant strength may spawn in this case.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 442.66666666667px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 440.66666666667px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Hill_Giant_Stool.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"The real Hill Giant Stool found in Act 1.\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e4/Hill_Giant_Stool.png/661px-Hill_Giant_Stool.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/e/e4/Hill_Giant_Stool.png/992px-Hill_Giant_Stool.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/e/e4/Hill_Giant_Stool.png/1322px-Hill_Giant_Stool.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"The real Hill Giant Stool found in Act 1.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e4/Hill_Giant_Stool.png/661px-Hill_Giant_Stool.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"441\" height=\"200\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/e/e4/Hill_Giant_Stool.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">The real Hill Giant Stool found in Act 1.</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 442px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 440px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"The fake Hill Giant Stool found in Act 3.\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/10/Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png/660px-Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/10/Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png/990px-Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/10/Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png/1320px-Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"The fake Hill Giant Stool found in Act 3.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/10/Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png/660px-Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"440\" height=\"200\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/10/Hill_Giant_Stool_Fake.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">The fake Hill Giant Stool found in Act 3.</div>\n\t\t</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714195431\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1422/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 20185/4194304 bytes